---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBasePath } from '../lib/site-paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn how Terapixel Games publishes fast, playable browser games with clear controls and honest release status."
>
  <div class="shell stack">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="page-title">About Terapixel Games</h1>
      <p class="page-copy">
        Terapixel Games is a small browser-game studio building quick arcade and puzzle sessions for players who want to
        open a tab, understand the goal, and start improving within the first minute.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content-grid" aria-label="Studio principles">
      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>What We Make</h2>
        <p>
          We publish lightweight web games with immediate controls, readable goals, and short repeatable runs. The current
          live library includes arcade, puzzle, and card games exported for modern desktop and mobile browsers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>How We Label Releases</h2>
        <p>
          Playable games have active launch links and game pages. Unreleased projects are clearly marked as coming soon,
          kept out of the sitemap, and do not pretend to offer a playable build.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>What Players Can Expect</h2>
        <p>
          Every live game page should explain the core loop, controls, and practical play tips before asking anyone to
          launch fullscreen. If something breaks, the Support and Contact pages provide a direct email channel.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>Editorial Standard</h2>
        <p>
          We keep site copy specific to games we operate, avoid fake download claims, and separate publisher information
          from ads, account tools, and shop experiments. The goal is a site that is useful with or without monetization.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="glass-panel text-panel" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact the Studio</h2>
      <p>
        For gameplay reports, privacy questions, or partnership inquiries, email
        <a href="mailto:support@terapixel.games">support@terapixel.games</a> or use the
        <a href={withBasePath('/support')}>Support page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
